SECTION  III:  TECHNICAL  SPECIFICATIONS  &  SCOPE  OF  WORKS   
The  project  scope  involves  the  construction  of:  1.  5  Blocks  of  G+8  (ground  plus  eight  stories)  
residential
 
apartments
 
totaling
 
400
 
units
 
(1-bedroom,
 
2-bedroom,
 
and
 
3-bedroom
 configurations).  2.  Internal  roads,  paving,  and  120-slot  parking  bays.  3.  Elevated  water  tanks  
and
 
borehole
 
drilling.
 
4.
 
Connection
 
to
 
the
 
main
 
municipal
 
sewer
 
line
 
and
 
electricity
 
grid.
 
 
 
SECTION  IV:  GENERAL  CONDITIONS  OF  CONTRACT  (GCC)  
4.1  Definitions.  In  this  Contract,  "the  Employer"  means  the  State  Department  for  Housing  
and
 
Urban
 
Development;
 
"the
 
Contractor"
 
means
 
the
 
firm
 
whose
 
tender
 
has
 
been
 
accepted;
 
"the
 
Works"
 
means
 
the
 
construction
 
described
 
in
 
Section
 
III;
 
"the
 
Contract
 
Price"
 
means
 
the
 
sum
 
stated
 
in
 
the
 
Letter
 
of
 
Acceptance.
 
4.2  Language  and  Law.  All  correspondence  shall  be  in  English.  This  Contract  shall  be  
governed
 
by
 
the
 
laws
 
of
 
Kenya.
 
4.3  Performance  Security.  The  successful  Tenderer  shall,  within  28  days  of  receipt  of  the  
Letter
 
of
 
Acceptance,
 
furnish
 
a
 
Performance
 
Security
 
equivalent
 
to
 
10%
 
of
 
the
 
Contract
 
Price
 
in
 
the
 
form
 
of
 
a
 
Bank
 
Guarantee,
 
valid
 
until
 
90
 
days
 
after
 
the
 
issuance
 
of
 
the
 
Certificate
 
of
 
Completion.
 
4.4  Insurance.  The  Contractor  shall,  at  its  own  expense,  take  out  and  maintain  in  the  joint  
names
 
of
 
the
 
Employer
 
and
 
the
 
Contractor:
 
(a)
 
Workmen's
 
Compensation
 
Insurance;
 
(b)
 
Third
 
Party
 
Liability
 
Insurance
 
of
 
not
 
less
 
than
 
KES
 
20,000,000;
 
(c)
 
All
 
Risks
 
Insurance
 
covering
 
the
 
Works,
 
plant,
 
and
 
materials
 
to
 
their
 
full
 
replacement
 
value.
 
4.5  Advance  Payment.  An  advance  payment  of  10%  of  the  Contract  Price  may  be  made  
upon
 
submission
 
of
 
an
 
unconditional
 
Advance
 
Payment
 
Guarantee
 
of
 
equal
 
value
 
from
 
a
 
bank
 
acceptable
 
to
 
the
 
Employer.
 
4.6  Time  for  Completion.  The  Works  shall  be  completed  within  24  (twenty-four)  months  
from
 
the
 
date
 
of
 
the
 
Site
 
Possession
 
Certificate.
 
4.7  Liquidated  Damages.  Should  the  Contractor  fail  to  complete  the  Works  within  the  Time  
for
 
Completion,
 
the
 
Contractor
 
shall
 
pay
 
Liquidated
 
Damages
 
of
 
0.1%
 
of
 
the
 
Contract
 
Price
 
per
 
day
 
of
 
delay,
 
up
 
to
 
a
 
maximum
 
of
 
10%
 
of
 
the
 
Contract
 
Price.
 
4.8  Defects  Liability  Period.  A  Defects  Liability  Period  of  12  months  shall  apply  from  the  
date
 
of
 
the
 
Certificate
 
of
 
Practical
 
Completion,
 
during
 
which
 
the
 
Contractor
 
shall
 
remedy
 
any
 
defects
 
at
 
its
 
own
 
cost.
 
4.9  Variations.  The  Employer's  representative  may  order  variations  to  the  Works.  No  
variation
 
shall
 
be
 
carried
 
out
 
without
 
prior
 
written
 
instruction.
 
Variations
 
exceeding
 
15%
 
of
 
the
 
original
 
Contract
 
Price
 
shall
 
require
 
approval
 
from
 
the
 
Public
 
Procurement
 
Regulatory
 
Authority.
 
4.10  Dispute  Resolution.  Disputes  shall  first  be  referred  to  the  Employer's  representative,  
then
 
to
 
adjudication
 
under
 
the
 
Kenya
 
Institute
 
of
 
Arbitrators
 
rules,
 
and
 
finally
 
to
 
arbitration
 
in
 
Nairobi
 
if
 
unresolved
 
within
 
90
 
days.
 
 SECTION  V:  SPECIAL  CONDITIONS  OF  CONTRACT  (SCC)  
5.1  Retention:  5%  of  each  Interim  Payment  Certificate  shall  be  retained,  half  released  upon  
Practical
 
Completion
 
and
 
half
 
upon
 
expiry
 
of
 
the
 
Defects
 
Liability
 
Period.
 
5.2  Interim  Payment  Certificates  shall  be  submitted  monthly  and  honored  within  30  days  of  
certification.
 
5.3  The  Contractor  shall  employ  a  minimum  of  60%  local  labor  from  Kisumu  County  
residents,
 
in
 
compliance
 
with
 
the
 
County
 
Government's
 
local
 
content
 
policy.
 
5.4  The  Contractor  shall  submit  monthly  progress  reports  including  photographic  evidence,  
updated
 
Gantt
 
charts,
 
and
 
material
 
delivery
 
records.
 
5.5  A  minimum  of  30%  of  subcontracted  works  (electrical,  plumbing,  painting)  shall  be  
awarded
 
to
 
firms
 
registered
 
under
 
AGPO
 
(Access
 
to
 
Government
 
Procurement
 
Opportunities).
 
 
